---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.7 · The Elf Finale" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-7" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.7</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The Elf Finale</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Follow the elf story from Regicide to Song of the Elves and open Prifddinas. Prepare one quest at a time, keeping the supplies and disguises you will reuse along the way.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Complete Regicide → Roving Elves → Mourning's End Part I → Mourning's End Part II → Song of the Elves, then enter Prifddinas ready for Chapter 3."
        stats={["All eight Song of the Elves skills at unboosted 70+", "60+ Ranged; 70 Prayer and Defence; 67 Sailing", "Iban Blast and phoenix necklaces for Seren; Thorgel's list if you lack a death talisman"]}
        unlocks={["Crystal equipment choice and Lletya access", "Death Altar and Temple of Light completion", "Prifddinas, crystal-city travel and activities"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before you begin:</strong> check the skill tab for unboosted <strong>70+ Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing and Woodcutting</strong>. Also confirm <strong>60+ Ranged, 70 Prayer, 70 Defence, Piety, 67 Sailing</strong>, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Ava's accumulator, upgraded Iban's staff, full Fairytale II, Making History and the completed quest chains from 2.1–2.6. The camphor-hulled skiff and other retained Chapter 2 kit stay banked where appropriate. If you are missing a level or unlock, return to its earlier training or quest step before continuing.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Tirannwn · the first crossing</div><h2>Prepare for a long trip and make tomorrow's naphtha today.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-regicide" number="1" title="Complete Regicide; bank a second barrel of naphtha">
        <p>Start with King Lathas in Ardougne Castle after <strong>Underground Pass</strong>; unboosted 70 Agility exceeds Regicide's 56 traversal gate. For the first Underground Pass/Tirannwn trip take a <strong>bow and arrows, two ropes (three is a comfortable buffer), spade, tinderbox, food, antipoison, teleports and combat gear</strong>. <strong>One cooked rabbit is a required hand-in</strong>; carry an axe to make a fire if the local fire is inconvenient. The forests have poison traps, hostile creatures and no convenient first-trip bank. Fight the level-110 Tyras guard from a safe distance with Ranged or Magic if your melee gear is modest. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Regicide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Regicide route map</a> is worth keeping open for the forest and Underground Pass crossings.</p>
        <p>At the Tyras camp collect <strong>at least three empty barrels</strong> in case one is lost, fill at least two with <strong>coal tar</strong> in the Poison Waste, and collect sulphur. After returning east, get <strong>limestone (not a limestone brick)</strong>, a <strong>pot, gloves, pestle and mortar</strong>, and a <strong>strip of cloth made from four balls of wool at a loom</strong>—a bolt of cloth is not the fuse. Keep the Big Book O' Bangs for the Chemist in Rimmington. At his fractionalising still, distil <strong>two separate barrels of coal tar</strong>: each uses roughly <strong>5–9 coal</strong>, so bring about 20 coal plus a buffer, hold pressure and heat in the green, and add coal gradually. Turn <em>one</em> naphtha into the barrel bomb with ground sulphur, pot of quicklime and cloth. <strong>Bank the second, unfinished barrel of naphtha for Mourning's End Part I.</strong> Do not add sulphur or quicklime to that one. Finish Regicide with the bomb and bank/regear afterward; keep that second barrel ready for the later quest.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace any missing bomb materials">
          <p>Use an ordinary bow and <strong>unpoisoned metal arrows</strong>; Lowe in Varrock sells bronze arrows, and a normal shortbow works. Buy ropes from Ned. Replace spade at the Falador estate agent, and tinderbox/bucket/pot at Lumbridge's general store. A regular plank helps with Underground Pass traps; cut a log and pay a sawmill 100 coins if none remains.</p>
          <p>Mine <strong>one raw limestone north of the Digsite</strong>. Buy or spin <strong>four balls of wool</strong> (Aemad in East Ardougne sells them), then use the <strong>loom at Falador Farm</strong> to make the strip of cloth. Buy a pestle and mortar at Jatix; if no hand-covering gloves are owned, pick up <strong>leather gloves inside Father Urhney's house</strong>. Wear them when making quicklime, and grind it into the pot.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>20 coal plus a small operating buffer from Ordan</strong>, if your bank is short after Smithing. The still can waste coal if its controls are mishandled: buy more coal only as needed until <strong>two finished naphtha barrels</strong> exist. If the reserved second barrel is later missing, collect a new empty barrel at Tyras camp, fill it in the Poison Waste, and repeat distillation before MEP1.</p>
          <p>Kill an <strong>Isafdar rabbit</strong> for raw rabbit and cook it on the fire east of Port Tyras, or on your own log fire. Cook another if it burns and keep <strong>one cooked rabbit for the catapult guard</strong>. Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>antipoison, prayer and ordinary restore doses</a> for the forest and crossings.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-roving" number="2" title="Complete Roving Elves; choose crystal shield by default">
        <p><strong>Regicide and Waterfall Quest</strong> are complete. Use Tirannwn access (or the Port Tyras charter) to find Islwyn and Eluned; carry food, antipoison and travel supplies for Isafdar. Check for <strong>Glarial's pebble</strong> from Waterfall Quest; retrieve it via the Tree Gnome Village dungeon if missing. Also stage a <strong>spade, rope and the Waterfall Dungeon key</strong> from its crates. For Glarial's Tomb, bank <strong>all weapons, armour, runes and ammunition</strong>—even a staff or rune stack blocks entry. Food and potions are allowed. Kill a level-84 Moss Guardian <strong>unarmed and unarmoured</strong> for the consecration seed, then use the Waterfall tomb and return to the elves. Bank/regear between the tomb and Tirannwn portions. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Roving_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <p>At the reward choice, <strong>crystal shield</strong> is the default immediate-use pick: it needs <strong>70 Defence and 50 Agility</strong>, which this route already has. The <strong>crystal bow</strong> needs <strong>70 Ranged and 50 Agility</strong>; the earlier training stopped at 60 Ranged. Bow is fine if your optional play reached 70 Ranged or you simply prefer it. <strong>You can continue the guide with either choice.</strong> See the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_shield" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">shield</a> and <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_bow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">bow</a> requirements.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the pebble and the two different keys locally">
          <p>If <strong>Glarial's pebble</strong> is missing, return to <strong>Golrie in the Tree Gnome Village dungeon</strong>; search the dungeon's crates for the key to reach him and ask for another pebble. That key is not the later Waterfall Dungeon key.</p>
          <p>Inside the <strong>Waterfall Dungeon</strong>, search the eastern room's crates for its own key before opening the western doors. Replace a rope from Ned and a spade from the Falador estate agent if needed. Food, prayer potions and antipoison can be refilled via the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion supply note</a>; bank prohibited combat equipment before entering Glarial's Tomb.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Mourner infiltration</div><h2>One disguise, two quests—do not lose the outfit.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-mep1" number="3" title="Complete Mourning's End Part I; retain every mourner piece">
        <p>Before starting, check <strong>Roving Elves, Big Chompy Bird Hunting and Sheep Herder</strong> complete, plus <strong>unboosted 60 Ranged and unboosted 50 Thieving</strong>. The earlier chapters cover these requirements. Stage the <strong>second barrel of naphtha from Regicide</strong>, two silk, bear fur (obtainable near Jorral's Outpost), one each of red/yellow/green/blue dye (buy at the Lletya Seamstress; extras cover missed shots), bucket of water, feather, magic log, soft leather, toad crunchies or premade t'd crunch, and travel/food. Get the quest-specific rotten apple north-west of the Mourner HQ and ogre bellows during the quest. Leave <strong>seven inventory spaces</strong> to receive the outfit. Before leaving, check that the magic log and spare naphtha barrel are still banked. The preparation note below explains how to replace either.</p>
        <p>Defeat a mourner near Arandar for the disguise; its potion lowers combat stats and Hitpoints to 20, so restore or regear before danger. Clean the bloody top with Tegid's soap and water; have Oronwen repair the trousers using the silk and bear fur. Wear the full mourner set to enter the West Ardougne HQ. The captive gnome fixes the device with the feather, leather, log and crunchies; dye swamp toads with bellows and use the device on all four sheep groups. Finally, combine the <strong>banked naphtha</strong> with the quest's rotten-apple mix, sieve it and cook the toxic naphtha on a <strong>range, not a fire</strong>; place the resulting powder in two grain sacks. Return to Arianwyn to <strong>finish MEP1 completely</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_I" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>KEEP THE FULL MOURNER OUTFIT, including the gas mask.</strong> Mourning's End Part II and Song of the Elves both use the disguise. Bank it intact after this quest; plague clothing is not a substitute.</div>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace every mourner-repair and device ingredient">
          <p>Buy <strong>two silk from the Al Kharid silk trader</strong> and obtain one bear fur by killing a bear near Jorral's Outpost or buying it from Baraek in Varrock. Buy <strong>red, yellow, blue and green dyes from Oronwen's Lletya shop</strong> once admitted; keep spare dye for missed sheep shots. Gerrant sells a feather. Kill a cow and have <strong>Ellis in Al Kharid tan one hide into soft leather</strong>. Buy <strong>premade t'd crunch from a Gnome waiter in the Grand Tree</strong>; it is an accepted substitute for self-cooked toad crunchies.</p>
          <p>If there is no <strong>magic log</strong>, your unboosted 70 Hunter already clears <strong>58 Hunter for nature implings</strong>. Enter Puro-Puro via the wheat field in Zanaris, take a butterfly net and impling jars from <strong>Elnock Inquisitor</strong>, and catch/open nature implings until one magic log is banked. Replace broken jars through Elnock as needed. The number of catches will vary; stop once you have the missing log. If you already have unboosted 75 Woodcutting, simply cut a magic tree instead.</p>
          <p>Take another <strong>ogre bellows from the chest in Rantz's cave</strong> if missing. The rotten apple is picked at the orchard north-west of Mourner HQ during the quest. If the second naphtha barrel was lost, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-regicide`}>Regicide barrel-and-still recovery</a>; coal tar and finished naphtha are different stages.</p>
          <p><strong>Lost mourner outfit later:</strong> kill another mourner by Arandar for its pieces, wash a new bloody top with <strong>Tegid's soap and a bucket of water</strong>, and have Oronwen mend ripped trousers with <strong>another two silk and bear fur</strong>. Recover the whole six-piece disguise including gas mask before MEP2 or Song; earlier repair materials were consumed.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-death-altar" number="4" title="Prepare Death Altar access before the Temple of Light">
        <p>First search the bank for a <strong>death talisman/tiara, catalytic talisman/tiara, or another currently valid altar-access item</strong> such as a Runecraft cape. Use one if you already own it. If you have played Guardians of the Rift, check whether you received a catalytic talisman. If you have no suitable access item, use Thorgel's <strong>50-item exchange</strong> to obtain a death talisman. His list is <strong>47 fixed items plus one randomly selected ticket, one book and one key</strong>. <strong>Bank check:</strong> collect one of each fixed entry still missing, in its listed form; Thorgel tells you which variant of each final three he wants. Bring them in multiple bank trips, not one impossible inventory. See the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II#The_Death_Altar" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current altar section</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Thorgel's complete 50-item collection list" label="If you need a death talisman">
          <p><strong>47 fixed items:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Babydragon bones, ball of wool, bronze bar, bronze med helm, bucket of milk, cake tin, cheese, chisel.</li>
            <li>Cooked meat, egg, facemask, fishing rod, flax, gold ring, hammer, iron axe, iron nails, iron pickaxe.</li>
            <li>Jug of wine, kebab, knife, leather boots, leather gloves, lobster pot, lockpick, necklace mould, needle, oak logs.</li>
            <li>Pie dish, plank, pot of flour, potato cactus, <strong>potatoes(10) sack</strong>, pure essence, redberries, rope.</li>
            <li>Rotten tomato, shears, skull, spade, swamp paste, thread, tinderbox, unicorn horn dust, vial of water, white apron, white berries.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Three assigned variants:</strong> one of <strong>archery ticket / new Agility arena ticket / Castle wars ticket</strong>; one of <strong>crumbling tome / slashed or battered book / Prifddinas' history</strong>; and one of <strong>jail key / dusty key / Witch's House door key</strong>. A POH bookcase can supply the books; the original collection places are below if you have not built one. Obtain only the ticket and key Thorgel actually assigns. An archery ticket comes from the Ranging Guild target range, a <em>new</em> Agility arena ticket from tagging a Brimhaven dispenser, or a Castle Wars ticket from that minigame. The jail key drops from the Taverley Dungeon jailer; the dusty key can be bought at the Legends' Guild or obtained from Velrak; Witch's House door key is under its front-door pot. For awkward fixed supplies, baby blue dragons in Taverley Dungeon provide babydragon bones, the Kalphite Lair has a potato-cactus ground spawn (bring rope and antipoison), and white berries grow around Isafdar. Check the bank before making any of these trips. The current <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> has exact directions.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Where to get Thorgel's missing items">
          <p><strong>Collect one of each fixed item, unnoted.</strong> The exceptions in appearance are still one hand-in: <strong>one iron nail</strong> and <strong>one full potatoes(10) sack</strong>, not ten loose potatoes. Check the list against your bank and obtain only the missing entries. Set aside the ingredients you still need for other quests or potions.</p>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Missing entries</th><th>Where to get them</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Ball of wool; bronze bar; gold ring</td><td>Buy wool from <strong>Aemad in East Ardougne</strong>, or shear/spin at Lumbridge. Buy copper/tin/gold ore from <strong>Ordan</strong>; smelt copper + tin into the bronze bar and gold ore into a gold bar. At <strong>5 Crafting</strong>, use the gold bar and Dommik's ring mould at a furnace for the plain gold ring.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Bronze med helm; iron axe; iron pickaxe; iron nail</td><td><strong>Peksa in Barbarian Village</strong> sells the helm, <strong>Bob in Lumbridge</strong> the axe, and <strong>Nurmof in the Dwarven Mine</strong> the pickaxe. Smith one iron bar into iron nails at <strong>19 Smithing</strong>; hand in one nail and keep the extras.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Bucket of milk; cheese; egg; pot of flour; cake tin; cooked meat</td><td>Buy the first four at the <strong>Culinaromancer's Chest</strong>. Buy a <strong>cake tin from a charter-ship trader</strong>. Kill a cow and cook one raw beef successfully for cooked meat; cooked chicken is a different item.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Chisel; hammer; needle; thread; shears; tinderbox; knife; spade</td><td>Lumbridge's general store supplies chisel/hammer/shears/tinderbox. <strong>Dommik in Al Kharid</strong> sells needle/thread. A <strong>knife spawns in Lumbridge Castle's kitchen</strong> and a <strong>spade at the Falador estate agent</strong>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Facemask; fishing rod; lobster pot; necklace mould; rope; lockpick</td><td>A <strong>Slayer master</strong> sells the facemask; <strong>Gerrant in Port Sarim</strong> sells the ordinary fishing rod and lobster pot; <strong>Dommik</strong> sells the mould; <strong>Ned in Draynor</strong> sells rope. <strong>Martin Thwait in the Rogues' Den</strong> sells lockpicks once 50 Agility/Thieving are met, as they are here.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Leather boots; leather gloves; white apron</td><td>Buy the boots and apron from <strong>Thessalia's Varrock clothes shop</strong>. Pick up leather gloves in <strong>Father Urhney's house in Lumbridge Swamp</strong>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Jug of wine; kebab; redberries; rotten tomato</td><td><strong>Fortunato in Draynor</strong> sells wine; <strong>Karim in Al Kharid</strong> sells kebabs. Pick redberries south-east of Varrock. Buy a rotten tomato from the <strong>crate by Varrock's pillory</strong>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Flax; oak logs; plank; pie dish; potatoes(10)</td><td>Pick flax in the <strong>Seers' Village flax field</strong> and chop one oak log. For the ordinary plank, cut a normal log and pay a sawmill <strong>100 coins</strong>. Make/fire a pie dish from one soft clay at <strong>Rimmington pottery, 7 Crafting</strong>. Buy an empty sack from <strong>Sarah's Farming shop south of Falador</strong>, pick ten potatoes in Lumbridge's field, and fill the sack.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pure essence; swamp paste; vial of water</td><td>Ask <strong>Aubury</strong> to teleport you to the essence mine and mine one pure essence (30 Mining; already exceeded). Buy paste from the <strong>Port Khazard general store</strong> and a vial of water from <strong>Jatix in Taverley</strong>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Babydragon bones; potato cactus</td><td>Kill a <strong>baby blue dragon in Taverley Dungeon</strong>; take a dusty key and anti-dragon shield for the surrounding dragon area. Pick up the <strong>potato cactus in the Kalphite Lair</strong>; take rope for its entrance and antipoison for the trip.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Skull; unicorn horn dust; white berries</td><td>Pick up a <strong>skull near Shayzien's graveyard dungeon entrance</strong>. Kill a unicorn south of Edgeville/near Barbarian Village and crush its horn with a pestle and mortar. Pick <strong>white berries in Isafdar north of the Elf Tracker, beyond the tripwire</strong>; bring antipoison rather than using a Wilderness spawn.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p><strong>Assigned ticket:</strong> for an archery ticket, pay the <strong>Ranging Guild Competition Judge</strong> and shoot the competition targets. For an <strong>Agility arena ticket</strong>, tag successive highlighted dispensers at Brimhaven; use a newly earned ticket, not a discontinued ticket or a Brimhaven voucher. For a <strong>Castle wars ticket</strong>, play completed matches until you have the requested ticket. Only do the activity named on Thorgel's list.</p>
          <p><strong>Assigned book:</strong> the <strong>crumbling tome</strong> is on the table in the building at the Barrows entrance; <strong>Prifddinas' history</strong> is in Lletya's bookcases near Arianwyn. For the <strong>battered/slashed book</strong>, search the east bookcase in the Seers' Village house with a cooking range, south of the anvils. Match the form Thorgel lists; using a knife on the battered book makes the slashed book and its key. You do not need to complete a new quest for this hand-in.</p>
          <p><strong>Assigned key:</strong> kill the <strong>Taverley Dungeon jailer</strong> for the jail key, use it to reach <strong>Velrak</strong> and ask for the dusty key if that is the assigned one, or take the <strong>Witch's House door key from under its front-door plant pot</strong>. Keep the other travelling supplies separate from any item already handed to Thorgel.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-mep2" number="5" title="Solve the Temple of Light and complete Mourning's End Part II">
        <p>Take <strong>full mourner gear, chisel, rope, food, Prayer restores, teleports and bank access</strong>; energy or stamina support is useful. Unboosted 70 Agility reduces obstacle trouble, while 70 Prayer plus <strong>Protect from Melee</strong> protects against the Temple's aggressive shadows. Start with Arianwyn in Lletya, enter the HQ in disguise, take Essyllt's <strong>new key</strong>, then reach the Temple through the dark-beast tunnels. Collect the journal and blackened crystal; chisel the crystal and have Arianwyn turn it into the <strong>newly made crystal</strong> needed at the end.</p>
        <p>The light puzzle has <strong>multiple sections</strong>: hand mirrors turn beams between pillars, coloured crystals change beams, and correctly coloured beams open doors to more mirrors, crystals and chests. Keep the mirrors/crystals you have collected and the newly made crystal; <strong>puzzle mirrors and crystals cannot be banked</strong>. Allow several free inventory slots early and up to roughly 13 near the last section. You can leave and regear between sections—the puzzle state persists—but follow the guide's <strong>cyan-door mirror position before teleporting out for Thorgel bank trips</strong>, or you can lock yourself out of the short return path. If using the 50-item route, give Thorgel his requested items over multiple trips, obtain the death talisman, return with the newly made crystal, and complete the altar sequence. If you brought a valid talisman, skip the exchange. Finish the quest and bank the mourner gear for Song. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mirror-by-mirror guide</a> for placements; keep it open while solving each section.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Restock between trips through the Temple">
          <p>Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-mep1`}>MEP1 recovery</a> if the full mourner outfit has been lost. Lumbridge's general store sells a chisel, Ned sells a new rope, and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion supply note</a> covers new prayer/energy doses if earlier elf trips used them.</p>
          <p>The new key, journal, mirrors, coloured crystals and final crystal are <strong>obtained during this quest</strong>. Keep them while following the current puzzle sequence. To enter the Death Altar, bring a suitable access item. If you have none, finish the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-death-altar`}>Thorgel collection</a> rather than waiting for an optional Guardians of the Rift reward.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Song of the Elves · final preparations</div><h2>Check the requirements and prepare the quest supplies.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Check these requirements before starting Song.</strong> Confirm <strong>Mourning's End Part II, Making History and Druidic Ritual</strong> complete, and unboosted <strong>70 Agility, 70 Construction, 70 Farming, 70 Herblore, 70 Hunter, 70 Mining, 70 Smithing and 70 Woodcutting</strong>. None of those eight level checks accepts a temporary boost. Return to the corresponding <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-6/`}>2.6 method</a> if you need more training. Song has no 80-Magic requirement.</div>
      <RouteStep id="i27-song-kit" number="6" title="Prepare the Song of the Elves items by quest phase">
        <p><strong>Ardougne disguise:</strong> steel full helm, steel platebody, steel platelegs, red dye, purple dye and one silk. <strong>Mourner phase:</strong> the <em>full</em> retained mourner set including gas mask (plague jacket/trousers do not work), plus a tinderbox. <strong>Waterfall offerings:</strong> rope, nature rune, flowers grown from mithril/adamant seeds <em>or one irit leaf</em>, an adamant chainbody (consumed), wine of Zamorak <em>or a Zamorak brew of any dose</em>, cabbage (can be picked during the quest), and a black knife <em>or black dagger</em>. <strong>Lletya/Prif preparation:</strong> one cadantine seed, seed dibber unless the relevant Barbarian Farming step is complete, runite bar, vial of water, pestle and mortar, hammer, pickaxe, then <strong>eight limestone bricks, saw, axe and spade</strong>. Lay these out by phase; you do not need every item in one inventory. Compare your supplies with the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">required-item list</a> and gather anything missing before starting.</p>
        <p><strong>Ironman sourcing:</strong> if no runite bar is banked, buy <strong>unnoted rune platelegs from Scavvo's Rune Store in the Champions' Guild for 64,000 coins</strong>, place them in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nest_(nice)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">nice nest atop Aldarin windmill</a>, log out or hop, then search the nest for <strong>one runite bar</strong>; no 85 Smithing or rare drop is needed. Check bank and Farming Guild seed vault for the <strong>cadantine seed</strong> first; if absent, use repeatable <strong>Master Farmer pickpockets</strong> (38 Thieving gate already cleared) or continue Farming Contracts/seed packs until one appears. The number of pickpockets or seed packs needed will vary. Buy the <strong>adamant chainbody at Wayne's Chains in southern Falador</strong> and the <strong>eight limestone bricks from Keldagrim's Stonemason</strong>. Ordinary armour shops cover steel pieces; Lletya's Seamstress or Aggie supplies dyes, and red plus blue makes purple. For the offerings, use a banked <strong>irit leaf</strong> if present; the note below gives a shop-bought flower alternative when it is absent; telegrab a wine of Zamorak from the non-Wilderness Asgarnia Chaos Temple if necessary; buy a <strong>black dagger at Varrock Swordshop</strong> if neither accepted black blade is banked. Check all items before the first story phase.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace the small Song supplies as well as its rare seed/bar">
          <p>For the steel disguise, smith <strong>ten new steel bars</strong> into a <strong>full helm (2 bars), platebody (5) and platelegs (3)</strong> at an anvil; all recipes fit the required unboosted 70 Smithing. Smelt Ordan's iron ore and coal at <strong>one iron + two coal per bar</strong>. Reuse your animated-armour set from the defender grind if all three pieces are still banked; make only any missing pieces.</p>
          <p>Buy the silk from the Al Kharid silk trader, and <strong>red and blue dyes from Oronwen in Lletya</strong>; mix red + blue for purple and keep a <strong>separate red dye</strong>. If there is no irit, buy <strong>mixed flowers from the Flower Girl in Miscellania</strong>; they are an accepted flower offering, so no seed-growing wait is needed. Buy the nature rune and the <strong>law rune for Telekinetic Grab</strong> at the Wizards' Guild, plus one air rune for the wine trip. Grab the wine from the <strong>non-Wilderness Chaos Temple north of Falador</strong>; bring food/teleport for the monks.</p>
          <p>Buy a seed dibber from Sarah's Farming shop, a vial of water and pestle and mortar from Jatix, hammer/tinderbox from Lumbridge's general store, saw from a sawmill, axe from Bob, pickaxe from Nurmof and rope from Ned; the Falador estate agent has a spade spawn. Take the cabbage found during the Waterfall section. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-mep1`}>MEP1 recovery note</a> supplies any missing mourner disguise pieces.</p>
          <p>The quest provides the <strong>elder cadantine and crystal-dust/inversion-potion sequence</strong> after you plant the one cadantine seed. Have the cadantine seed and runite bar ready before starting; ordinary cadantine herbs do not replace the quest plant.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-seren-kit" number="7" title="Prepare Iban, phoenix necklaces and stackable nightshade for Seren">
        <p>The default no-brews setup is <strong>upgraded Iban's staff with Iban Blast</strong> on the standard spellbook (<strong>50 Magic; five fire runes and one death rune per cast</strong>), around <strong>15–20 phoenix necklaces</strong>, <strong>20+ stackable nightshade</strong>, <strong>2–4 Prayer potions</strong>, <strong>1–2 multi-heal food options</strong> such as Guthix rest, and <strong>50+ throwing knives or chinchompas</strong> for the 1-HP healing pillars. If neither projectile is banked, smith <strong>10 iron bars into 50 iron knives</strong> at 22 Smithing; do not rely on an optional chinchompa catch. Bring enough Iban charges and runes for repeated attempts, an emergency teleport, and Magic-accuracy gear (roughly +50 Magic attack if your level/gear is modest). These are preparation ranges from the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fragment_of_Seren#Phoenix_necklaces" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current low-level strategy</a>, so adjust the amount if you already know a smaller stock is enough for your attempts.</p>
        <p><strong>Necklaces:</strong> check banked diamonds and existing phoenix necklaces first. At <strong>56 Crafting</strong>, use a diamond, gold bar and necklace mould on a furnace; at <strong>57 Magic</strong>, Lvl-4 Enchant each diamond necklace with <strong>one cosmic and ten earth runes</strong>. If short on diamonds, mine repeatable <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shilo_Village_mine" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Shilo Village gem rocks</a> (already unlocked) or spend banked Shooting Star stardust on <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bag_full_of_gems" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">40-gem bags</a> at 300 stardust each. Diamond yield varies; stop when you have enough to finish your necklace stock.</p>
        <p><strong>Nightshade:</strong> check bank and seed vault for <strong>belladonna seeds</strong> and plant them early at the <strong>Draynor Manor or Auburnvale belladonna patch</strong>; unboosted 70 Farming clears its 63 gate. Harvest with gloves. One crop gives <strong>6–18 stackable nightshade</strong>, so two good harvests may cover 20, but check the actual yield and replant if short. If no seed is banked, catch <strong>nature implings</strong> (58 Hunter, already cleared; their jars can contain belladonna seed) or repeat <strong>Master Farmer pickpockets / Farming Contracts</strong> until one appears. Check the bank first, then gather only the seeds you still need. Free cave nightshade is an emergency fallback, but it is <strong>unstackable</strong> and displaces necklace/restore slots. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nightshade" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nightshade reference</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Refill charges, finished necklaces and doses for the next attempt">
          <p>Check gold and enchantment runes as well: buy gold ore from <strong>Ordan</strong>, smelt one gold bar per missing diamond necklace, and buy a necklace mould from <strong>Dommik</strong>. <strong>Baba Yaga</strong> sells cosmics, and an elemental rune shop supplies the <strong>ten earth runes per enchantment</strong>. The finished item is a <strong>phoenix necklace</strong>; do not bring an unenchanted diamond necklace into the boss inventory.</p>
          <p>Buy death and fire runes from <strong>Aubury</strong>, and check the upgraded Iban's staff's <strong>remaining charges</strong> before each attempt. Recharge at the <strong>Flames of Zamorak well in the Underground Pass</strong>, or pay the Dark Mage outside the Pass for the missing charges if you prefer his service. Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer potions</a> from current herbs and snape grass. Make Guthix rest using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-one-small`}>One Small Favour tea recipe</a>; buy/gather its herbs again if they were consumed.</p>
          <p>For missing belladonna seeds, the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-mep1`}>Puro-Puro equipment and nature-impling method</a> also works for this drop. Plant only enough crops to meet the <strong>remaining stackable-nightshade requirement</strong>, with gloves to harvest. Cave nightshade takes one inventory slot per item, so use the farmed version for this setup when possible.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">The rebellion and final fight</div><h2>Bank between story phases; enter Seren with a rehearsed cycle.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-song" number="8" title="Complete Song of the Elves; unlock Prifddinas">
        <p>Start with Arianwyn in Lletya, then follow the Ardougne/Edmond and Elena story using the steel knight disguise. Move through the West Ardougne rebellion in mourner gear and the Waterfall Dungeon's six-offering pillar puzzle. Bank between these phases; do not drag all quest items through every fight. In the Lletya/Prif preparation, plant the cadantine seed, use the runite bar and hammer on the elderly elf's exoskeleton, and make the inversion potion with the elder cadantine and crystal dust. The Grand Library and city preparation lead into hostile combat. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full quest guide</a>.</p>
        <p>For the <strong>Arianwyn</strong> fight, take sensible food/restores and Ranged or Melee gear; move off his orange ground attacks and watch the purple attack that disables Prayer. Regear before the <strong>Underground Pass siege and Essyllt</strong>: multiple enemies make Prayer, food and supply management important. The quest moves toward Seren after the siege; you can <strong>teleport out after the transition/cutscene to bank and build the dedicated Seren inventory</strong> rather than force the boss with leftover siege supplies. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">phase guide</a> gives exact dialogue and puzzle clicks.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Unsafe-death storage:</strong> items lost during Song's major instanced fights can be reclaimed from the <strong>Rebel Scout for 80,000 coins</strong> (the fee may come from your bank). For Seren, the Scout appears <strong>outside the boss entrance</strong>. Reclaim items <strong>before dying anywhere else</strong>; another unsafe death while the Scout still holds them can delete that stash. Do not use a new fight as a recovery shortcut. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Item_Retrieval_Service" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current retrieval rule</a>.</div>
        <p><strong>Understand Seren's repeat:</strong> keep <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> up for normal projectiles (their max drops to 3+3); on her first special she teleports you beside her, so step away before the rapid melee hits. On the second, attack the <strong>lighter-coloured real clone</strong>. On the third, rapidly tag each red <strong>1-HP healing pillar</strong> with knives/chins so she cannot heal through your Iban damage. Between specials, cast Iban Blast and maintain Prayer/charges. Her fourth special teleports you in front of her and queues a hit for almost your maximum HP. Let normal damage bring you to a controlled low HP early (the Wiki suggests about 30–40 HP initially), then <strong>after the fourth teleport, equip a fresh phoenix necklace and right-click Eat the stackable nightshade during the attack wind-up, before the hitsplat</strong>. Nightshade self-damage must carry you from <em>above</em> to <em>at or below</em> 20% of maximum HP to trigger the necklace. That activation clears the queued near-max hit even though its animation finishes, and the necklace then heals about 30% maximum HP. At 20+ current HP nightshade deals 15, so aim around <strong>20% of maximum HP plus 10–15 HP</strong>; keep enough margin to survive normal attacks and heal if you drift outside that window. Practice the timing against the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fragment_of_Seren#Phoenix_necklaces" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki animation/strategy</a>; heal, restore Prayer and use another necklace for the next cycle. Teleport out if supplies or timing are not safe. Blood Blitz, brews or a better powered staff can simplify the fight <em>if already owned</em>, but the Iban setup above works without them.</p>
        <p>After the Fragment, follow the final dialogue and <strong>finish Song of the Elves completely</strong>—do not stop at the boss kill. Claim <strong>four quest points and 40,000 XP in each of the eight required skills</strong>, plus <strong>Prifddinas</strong>, its port/crystal-city travel and access to the Gauntlet, Zalcano and elven dungeon/resources to explore when you choose. Check your new skill levels after claiming the rewards.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Restock for the next quest phase or boss attempt">
          <p>Before starting a story phase, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-song-kit`}>complete quest kit and recovery note</a>. Before Seren or a retry, use the separate <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/#i27-seren-kit`}>Seren supply check</a> so earlier siege food, spent necklaces and consumed doses are replaced. The quest's local crystal, seed and potion items come from its dialogue and collection steps; keep them until the quest asks you to use them.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 2 complete</div>
        <h3>Prifddinas is open. Stop here.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests/access:</strong> Regicide, Roving Elves, Mourning's End I/II and Song of the Elves complete; <strong>Prifddinas unlocked</strong>. Also retain full Fairytale II, Making History, Defender of Varrock, Dream Mentor, A Tail of Two Cats and the earlier quest chains.</li>
          <li><strong>Unboosted levels:</strong> at least <strong>70</strong> in all eight Song skills (Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing, Woodcutting); <strong>70 Prayer, 70 Defence, 60 Ranged, 51 Slayer and 67 Sailing</strong>. Check the skill tab for your new levels after the quest rewards.</li>
          <li><strong>Combat/travel kit:</strong> Piety, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Helm of Neitiznot, Proselyte, Ava's accumulator, upgraded Iban's staff, camphor-hulled skiff, Ectophial, Drakan's medallion, Blisterwood flail, Salve (e), Book of the Dead and the Weiss herb patch.</li>
          <li><strong>Save for Chapter 3:</strong> Path of Glouphrie plus its <strong>unboosted 56 Slayer</strong> catch-up; Curse of Arrav; Sailing beyond 67; Construction beyond 70; Chapter 3-specific Mining, Smithing and ship upgrades; and Mage Arena II if still desired. You can begin Chapter 3 with these still unfinished.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The optional kitten → cat → death-rune loop introduced after Ardougne Easy is now entirely <strong>up to you</strong>: use it only when a kitten fits your play and the runes are worth the attention. Check your coins and runes before future purchases, whether you continue raising cats or stop here. Continue to <strong>3.1 Slayer Foundation &amp; While Guthix Sleeps</strong>; check your skills and supplies at the start of that chapter.</p>
      </section>

